{"results":[{"url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2021/06/07/hunter-bidens-laptop-april-16-2015-dinner/","final_url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2021/06/07/hunter-bidens-laptop-april-16-2015-dinner/","title":"Analysis | Hunter Biden’s laptop: The April 16, 2015, dinner","description":"A recent report suggested that then-Vice President Joe Biden attended a dinner with Hunter Biden’s business associates. But two participants say he just briefly stopped by to meet with a Greek Orthodox priest.","language":"en","text":"Democracy Dies in Darkness\n\nAnalysis by  Glenn Kessler\n\n*This article, first published in 2021, has been updated.*\n\nWhen the New York Post released emails last fall from what it claimed was Hunter Biden’s laptop, The Fact Checker produced an explainer that turned out to be one of the most-read articles in our 13-year history. A key question we examined was whether Hunter Biden, President Biden’s son, arranged for a top executive at a Ukrainian energy firm to meet with the then-vice president when he was in charge of U.S. policy toward Ukraine. The date in question: April 16, 2015.\n\n---","author":"Glenn Kessler","published_date":"2021-06-07T07:00:43.646Z","latency_ms":588.4779340121895,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}